  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. Enharmonic notes sound the same in equal temperament.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q2. Spelling follows key context.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. Augmented fourth equals tritone.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Diminished fifth equals tritone.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. Neutral thirds appear in some Arabic and Turkish scales.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. Advanced analysis requires correct enharmonic spelling.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. Quarter tones are outside standard twelve-tone set.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Compound intervals can be reduced modulo octave for analysis.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. Interval skills support modal analysis.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Regional units extend—not replace—this framework.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Chromatic semitone is one half step.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Diminished seventh spans nine semitones.\n\n**Answer:** True",
